      "writtenOn": "2026-04-14T15:26:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I looked into it, and I don\u0027t think it\u0027s feasible. This relies on 2417218f2f23 (\"KVM: arm64: Get rid of __kvm_get_mdcr_el2() and related warts\"), which completely changes how kvm_host_data is initialized. It introduces a new centralized boot-time function called kvm_init_host_debug_data() to cache PMU counters and debug states. 38131c02a53f simply hooks into this new infrastructure to cache the HAS_SPE and HAS_TRBE flags.\n\nBackporting 2417218f2f23 would require us to drag in even more unrelated structural refactoring patches (modifying PMU and MDCR_EL2 handling).\n\nI updated the commit message to reflect that. What do you think?",
